tle":137,"path":138,"stem":139},"Self-hosting","\u002Fdocs\u002Fself-hosting","docs\u002F14.self-hosting",{"title":141,"path":142,"stem":143},"Security (allowedTools)","\u002Fdocs\u002Fsecurity","docs\u002F15.security",{"id":145,"title":10,"body":146,"description":486,"extension":487,"links":488,"meta":489,"navigation":490,"path":11,"seo":491,"stem":12,"__hash__":492},"docs\u002Fdocs\u002F01.introduction.md",{"type":147,"value":148,"toc":479},"minimark",[149,169,174,181,218,226,230,339,343,346,367,374,381,385,395,434,438],[150,151,152,156,157,160,161,164,165,168],"p",{},[153,154,155],"strong",{},"sched"," is a cron scheduler done right: ",[153,158,159],{},"reliable delivery",", ",[153,162,163],{},"run history",", and a\n",[153,166,167],{},"web UI"," — self-hosted, queue-based, polyglot-ready.",[170,171,173],"h2",{"id":172},"why-sched","Why sched",[150,175,176,177,180],{},"\"Fire and forget\" is not enough for a scheduler. sched's promise — ",[153,178,179],{},"the scheduler knows\neverything about every run",":",[182,183,184,196,202,208],"ul",{},[185,186,187,190,191,195],"li",{},[153,188,189],{},"Input"," — with what parameters the task was invoked (",[192,193,194],"code",{},"data",")",[185,197,198,201],{},[153,199,200],{},"Progress"," — 0–100 progress and captured stdout\u002Fstderr log",[185,203,204,207],{},[153,205,206],{},"Outcome"," — JSON result, error, artifacts (S3 keys, email receipts, URLs)",[185,209,210,213,214,217],{},[153,211,212],{},"Lifecycle"," — ",[192,215,216],{},"queued → running → succeeded | failed | cancelled",", timestamps, duration",[150,219,220,221,225],{},"Runs survive restarts, locks are reaped, and every run is recorded in the storage — SQLite\nby default, or MySQL\u002FMariaDB, Postgres or Mongo when history must live in an existing\ndatabase (each is a separate package, see ",[222,223,75],"a",{"href":224},"storage",").",[170,227,229],{"id":228},"key-features","Key features",[182,231,232,242,269,279,289,299,313,322,331],{},[185,233,234,237,238,241],{},[153,235,236],{},"Cron scheduling"," with timezone support (",[192,239,240],{},"tz",") and DST-safe next-run calculation",[185,243,244,247,248,251,252,160,254,160,257,160,260,160,263,160,266],{},[153,245,246],{},"Run history"," (",[192,249,250],{},"RunRecord","): ",[192,253,194],{},[192,255,256],{},"result",[192,258,259],{},"error",[192,261,262],{},"progress",[192,264,265],{},"log",[192,267,268],{},"artifacts",[185,270,271,274,275,278],{},[153,272,273],{},"Pluggable storage"," — SQLite first (in ",[192,276,277],{},"@schedjs\u002Fcore","), MySQL\u002FMariaDB, Postgres and\nMongo as separate adapter packages, all with a contract test-suite",[185,280,281,284,285,288],{},[153,282,283],{},"Polyglot runners"," — HTTP, Docker, and any custom runner you write against the ",[192,286,287],{},"Runner"," contract",[185,290,291,294,295,195],{},[153,292,293],{},"Embedded mode"," — schedule in-process functions with the internal runner; no daemon, no Docker (see ",[222,296,298],{"href":297},"quick-start#1-embedded-schedule-functions-in-process","quick start",[185,300,301,213,304,307,308,312],{},[153,302,303],{},"Retries with backoff",[192,305,306],{},"retry: { maxAttempts, backoffMs, multiplier }"," per task; a ",[309,310,311],"em",{},"persistent"," failure is one where retries ran out",[185,314,315,213,318,321],{},[153,316,317],{},"Idempotent dispatch",[192,319,320],{},"x-sched-run-id"," on the wire; workers dedupe by run id",[185,323,324,213,327,330],{},[153,325,326],{},"Async runs",[192,328,329],{},"202 accepted"," + polling for long-running jobs",[185,332,333,335,336,338],{},[153,334,117],{}," + ",[153,337,167],{}," (web components) — see runs, tasks, status",[170,340,342],{"id":341},"three-ways-to-run","Three ways to run",[150,344,345],{},"Pick by scale — the engine underneath is the same, so run history, retries and alerts\nwork on every path:",[347,348,349,355,361],"ol",{},[185,350,351,354],{},[153,352,353],{},"Embedded"," — schedule functions in-process, zero infra (SQLite file + handlers).",[185,356,357,360],{},[153,358,359],{},"Standalone daemon"," — own process with HTTP\u002FDocker workers, admin UI, alerts.",[185,362,363,366],{},[153,364,365],{},"Docker"," — the daemon in a container, compose-friendly, self-hosting.",[150,368,369,370,373],{},"See ",[222,371,18],{"href":372},"quick-start"," to run your first task on any of them.",[150,375,376,377,380],{},"sched is not the right tool for every scheduling problem. ",[222,378,14],{"href":379},"comparison"," puts it\nnext to BullMQ, Bull, Kue, Bee, pg-boss and Agenda and says where it wins, where it loses,\nand what to use instead.",[170,382,384],{"id":383},"architecture","Architecture",[386,387,392],"pre",{"className":388,"code":390,"language":391},[389],"language-text","            tasks.json (desired state)\n                    │ sync\n                    ▼\n   ┌────────────┐   tick\u002Fwatchdog\u002Fpoll    ┌───────────────────────────────┐\n   │   Engine   │ ──────────────────────▶ │      Runners (execution)      │\n   │ (scheduler)│   claim → run → record  │ http · docker · process · ssh │\n   │            │                         │ mcp · internal · custom       │\n   └─────┬──────┘                         └───────────────────────────────┘\n         │ storage seam\n         ▼\n   ┌───────────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │        Storage        │    │  Daemon (CLI + Admin API + UI)       │\n   │ sqlite\u002Fmysql\u002Fpg\u002Fmongo │    │ --admin-port · SCHED_ADMIN_KEY       │\n   └───────────────────────┘    └──────────────────────────────────────┘\n","text",[192,393,390],{"__ignoreMap":394},"",[182,396,397,403,416,424],{},[185,398,399,402],{},[153,400,401],{},"Engine"," — deterministic tick loop + zombie watchdog over the storage seam. Claims due\ntasks, dispatches to the runner, records outcomes, reaps stale locks.",[185,404,405,407,408,411,412,415],{},[153,406,35],{}," — own ",[309,409,410],{},"how"," a task runs. HTTP (request\u002Fresponse, sync or ",[192,413,414],{},"accepted"," + poll),\nDocker (container spawn), or your own in-process function.",[185,417,418,420,421,423],{},[153,419,75],{}," — the ",[192,422,75],{}," contract: tasks, runs, locking. SQLite, MySQL\u002FMariaDB,\nPostgres and Mongo implement it.",[185,425,426,429,430,433],{},[153,427,428],{},"Daemon"," — loads ",[192,431,432],{},"tasks.json"," (desired state), syncs it, runs the engine, serves the\nadmin API and the web UI.",[170,435,437],{"id":436},"where-to-go-next","Where to go next",[182,439,440,445,450,458,466,472],{},[185,441,442,444],{},[222,443,14],{"href":379}," — sched next to BullMQ, Agenda, pg-boss and friends",[185,446,447,449],{},[222,448,18],{"href":372}," — run your first scheduled task in 3 minutes",[185,451,452,420,455,457],{},[222,453,23],{"href":454},"tasks",[192,456,432],{}," format and scheduling",[185,459,460,463,464],{},[222,461,27],{"href":462},"runs"," — the run lifecycle and ",[192,465,250],{},[185,467,468,471],{},[222,469,35],{"href":470},"runners\u002Fhttp"," — HTTP \u002F Docker \u002F custom runners",[185,473,474,478],{},[222,475,477],{"href":476},"protocol","Protocol"," — the wire contract between sched and workers",{"title":394,"searchDepth":21,"depth":21,"links":480},[481,482,483,484,485],{"id":172,"depth":21,"text":173},{"id":228,"depth":21,"text":229},{"id":341,"depth":21,"text":342},{"id":383,"depth":21,"text":384},{"id":436,"depth":21,"text":437},"What sched is and how it works","md",null,{},true,{"title":10,"description":486},"LNuopCClOlWw2LBj_2av9FdDu8Q8b3_OYKLQpBBpkO4",[494,496],{"title":5,"path":6,"stem":7,"description":495,"order":8,"children":-1},"Version history — release notes for every sched wave, newest first",{"title":14,"path":15,"stem":16,"description":497,"children":-1},"sched next to the Node.js job schedulers and queues it is usually weighed against — BullMQ (and its commercial BullMQ-Pro), Bull, Kue, Bee, pg-boss and Agenda",1789974206542]